  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 8 is the longest at Buffalo Ridge at 479 feet — a par 3 that climbs with the course's best elevation and rewards the blind thrower with the mountain views below. It's the hole that defines the course: rugged, scenic, and honest about what desert disc golf asks of you.",

  "localTips": "Bring water and sturdy shoes — the terrain is rugged and the blind holes mean hiking. The Alpha-9 loop (holes A–I) adds nine more for a full 27. Free to play with restrooms on site; the views are the real reward.",

